Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:11:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] CompositionEngine: Mark SystemUI's screen decoration as
 an RC mask

Qualcomm's display engine can draw the rounded screen corners itself
(the DSPP RC block), leaving the source pipes to real layers, but only
for layers marked through the vendor IDisplayConfig service. CLO's
SurfaceFlinger does that, AOSP's doesn't. On SM7435, with three source
pipes, the two corner overlays otherwise push transition frames into
GPU composition.

With ro.sf.screen_decor_mask set, call IDisplayConfig.setLayerAsMask
for the ScreenDecorHwcOverlay layer when its HWC layer is created on
the primary display. The call is a raw binder transaction (the 28th
method; stable AIDL only appends), so no QTI interface library is
needed.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HCu2kUrLkzjzZJEZ6mCKqM
---
 .../CompositionEngine/Android.bp              |  1 +
 .../CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp         | 40 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 41 insertions(+)

